<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quanah Parker</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1845–1911</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quanah Parker was a war leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwahadi">Kwahadi Comanche</a>, the son of Peta Nocona and the captive Cynthia Ann Parker. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-war">Red River War</a> he led the last free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> band to surrender at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-sill">Fort Sill</a> in 1875. On the reservation he became the Comanche's principal leader, a successful rancher and a promoter of the peyote religion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quanah-parker.jpg" alt="Quanah Parker" width="320" height="793" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel P. Sink of Vernon Texas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quanah_Parker_c1890.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
